kosha lead

  -- Pb. proton-82. period 6, post-transition metal. valence: 2 or 4.
  -- dense, soft, malleable. low melting point (327°C). poor conductor.
  -- historically: plumbing (Latin plumbum), paint, solder, batteries.
  -- lead-acid battery: Pb + PbO2 + H2SO4 → electrical energy.
  -- radiation shielding: high density absorbs X-rays and gamma rays.
  -- toxic: accumulates in bones (replaces calcium). neurotoxin.
  -- end of the radioactive decay chains: U-238 → Pb-206, U-235 → Pb-207.

